       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and I don't know of any recognized protocol that gives amlodipine 50 mg daily. That dose is far above the 10 mg maximum, and an overdose can cause refractory hypotension and shock. Monitoring would catch the harm only after it started. With a risk that severe, a statement I can't check isn't enough for me to submit the order.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter it through your usual prescriber workflow.** If the protocol is documented and pharmacist-reviewed, the order can go through the EHR's high-dose override and pharmacy verification. That route has the protocol on record and the right people accountable for it.\n- **I can enter a dose within the labeled range now.** That would be 10 mg by mouth once daily, and I can add a note such as \"titrate per protocol, pending pharmacy review.\"\n- **I can enter a different dose or schedule** if the protocol is actually something else, for example a typo or a split dose.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
